WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:37.920
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:38.190 --> 01:44.030
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.140 --> 01:46.880
[Episode 19]

4
01:47.150 --> 01:49.360
[Starry Night] [Prosperous Dynasty]

5
01:49.430 --> 01:55.259
[Kindly close the door behind you]

6
01:55.289 --> 01:58.229
[Medical Staff Only]

7
01:58.350 --> 02:06.550
[Quiet]

8
02:00.070 --> 02:00.870
Hello.

9
02:01.200 --> 02:02.840
I'm Wang Chao, deputy chief

10
02:02.840 --> 02:04.480
of the Municipal Criminal Investigation Division.

11
02:04.480 --> 02:05.200
Doctor,

12
02:05.400 --> 02:07.070
how's Du Fang doing?

13
02:07.590 --> 02:09.250
He's out of immediate danger,

14
02:09.310 --> 02:10.080
but it's too early

15
02:10.080 --> 02:11.470
to tell how well

16
02:11.800 --> 02:12.680
he'll recover.

17
02:14.360 --> 02:15.280
Now that he's alive,

18
02:15.280 --> 02:16.590
it changes

19
02:16.590 --> 02:17.800
the nature of things.

20
02:18.150 --> 02:19.840
Anyway, thank you.

21
02:20.280 --> 02:21.140
It's all right.

22
02:21.470 --> 02:23.400
There's something I need to ask you, though.

23
02:23.400 --> 02:25.030
Before he was shot,

24
02:25.150 --> 02:27.190
the patient kept insisting he was innocent.

25
02:27.190 --> 02:28.280
That's impossible.

26
02:28.280 --> 02:29.590
He assaulted his supervisor at work.

27
02:29.590 --> 02:31.240
Plenty of people saw it.

28
02:32.000 --> 02:34.150
I'm not questioning your investigation.

29
02:34.150 --> 02:35.190
It's just that

30
02:35.190 --> 02:36.630
during surgery,

31
02:36.710 --> 02:37.870
we discovered

32
02:37.870 --> 02:39.079
a tumor

33
02:39.280 --> 02:40.480
in the temporal lobe.

34
02:40.520 --> 02:41.280
Damage to the temporal lobe

35
02:41.280 --> 02:42.840
can cause personality changes,

36
02:42.840 --> 02:43.840
erratic behavior,

37
02:43.840 --> 02:45.870
and even psychiatric symptoms.

38
02:47.680 --> 02:48.520
What does that mean?

39
02:48.520 --> 02:49.840
That there's something wrong

40
02:49.840 --> 02:51.030
with his brain?

41
02:51.590 --> 02:52.430
That he

42
02:52.590 --> 02:54.250
didn't know what he was doing?

43
02:54.280 --> 02:55.540
That's a possibility.

44
02:55.910 --> 02:57.400
So I'd recommend

45
02:57.800 --> 03:00.060
having him undergo another evaluation.

46
03:03.820 --> 03:09.280
[Bicycle Parking]

47
03:09.390 --> 03:10.240
[Operating Department]

48
03:12.360 --> 03:14.240
This is Dr. Liu Zhengliang,

49
03:14.130 --> 03:23.380
[Accessible Route—Please Keep Clear]

50
03:14.310 --> 03:15.840
the doctor who chose to operate

51
03:15.840 --> 03:17.120
on a patient even

52
03:17.120 --> 03:18.960
while being held hostage by criminals.

53
03:18.960 --> 03:21.120
These two are reporters from the provincial newspaper.

54
03:21.120 --> 03:22.430
They'd like to do

55
03:22.430 --> 03:23.870
a feature interview with you.

56
03:23.870 --> 03:24.280
Hello.

57
03:24.280 --> 03:25.000
Hello.

58
03:25.120 --> 03:26.430
Hi, hi.

59
03:28.030 --> 03:29.360
I've barely been back a day,

60
03:29.360 --> 03:30.910
and I've already got so much to deal with.

61
03:30.910 --> 03:32.520
I still have to go over everything with Chief Physician Tong.

62
03:32.520 --> 03:34.430
Can you give me a minute to catch my breath?

63
03:34.430 --> 03:35.960
This is the Zhang family's thank-you banner.

64
03:35.960 --> 03:37.360
It got a little blood on it,

65
03:37.360 --> 03:38.760
and I had them clean it up.

66
03:38.910 --> 03:41.040
Take it back and hang it in your office.

67
03:51.560 --> 03:52.360
See?

68
03:53.710 --> 03:56.570
This is a rare opportunity for some good publicity.

69
03:59.630 --> 04:00.960
You know perfectly well

70
04:01.630 --> 04:03.760
how much this hospital is struggling.

71
04:03.910 --> 04:06.240
Guess I came back at the worst possible time.

72
04:06.240 --> 04:07.800
Quite the opposite.

73
04:08.110 --> 04:10.370
Didn't you save another life just today?

74
04:15.800 --> 04:16.560
All right.

75
04:18.750 --> 04:20.149
Where do you want to talk?

76
04:21.070 --> 04:22.600
How about the conference room?

77
04:22.600 --> 04:24.330
Let's use the conference room.

78
04:25.070 --> 04:25.630
Let's go.

79
04:25.720 --> 04:26.780
Let's go. Let's go.

80
04:28.630 --> 04:29.430
Dr. Liu,

81
04:29.510 --> 04:30.310
you said earlier

82
04:29.670 --> 04:33.170
[Healing pain with compassion, lighting up hope with dedication]

83
04:30.310 --> 04:31.950
that the fugitive's criminal behavior

84
04:31.950 --> 04:35.190
might have been caused by some kind of physiological abnormality.

85
04:35.190 --> 04:35.990
That's right.

86
04:36.120 --> 04:37.000
Of course, it's only

87
04:37.000 --> 04:39.040
a possibility I've raised.

88
04:39.159 --> 04:40.810
We'll need to investigate further to verify it.

89
04:40.810 --> 04:46.940
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

90
04:41.480 --> 04:43.000
If your theory turns out to be correct,

91
04:43.000 --> 04:44.720
you'll have saved

92
04:44.720 --> 04:46.240
more than one life.

93
04:49.830 --> 04:50.630
Well,

94
04:51.159 --> 04:52.159
honestly,

95
04:52.190 --> 04:54.430
I didn't think that far ahead at the time.

96
04:54.430 --> 04:55.560
You're very modest.

97
04:55.750 --> 04:56.560
So, what made you

98
04:56.560 --> 04:59.020
decide to become a doctor in the first place?

99
05:08.070 --> 05:09.530
When my uncle passed away,

100
05:10.720 --> 05:11.720
I realized

101
05:12.950 --> 05:14.600
how much I hated feeling helpless

102
05:14.600 --> 05:15.920
in the face of death.

103
05:29.820 --> 05:32.400
[Memorial Hall]

104
05:35.750 --> 05:36.560
Well,

105
05:38.950 --> 05:41.120
my college entrance exam score was high enough to get me into medical school.

106
05:41.120 --> 05:41.870
I didn't give it much thought

107
05:41.870 --> 05:43.730
when I filled out my application.

108
05:45.490 --> 05:51.310
[Medical Staff Only]

109
05:55.560 --> 05:56.870
What are you waiting for?

110
05:56.870 --> 05:57.680
For you.

111
05:58.070 --> 05:59.610
Let's grab something to eat

112
06:00.040 --> 06:00.950
and celebrate.

113
06:01.720 --> 06:02.750
Celebrate what?

114
06:03.240 --> 06:06.310
Come on, it's a once-in-a-lifetime thing!

115
06:06.390 --> 06:07.390
Maybe the only time

116
06:07.390 --> 06:09.000
in your life

117
06:09.000 --> 06:10.510
you'll ever operate on a patient

118
06:10.510 --> 06:11.240
who's been shot in the head.

119
06:11.240 --> 06:13.640
Don't you think that's worth celebrating?

120
06:14.560 --> 06:15.360
Sure.

121
06:15.480 --> 06:17.210
Let's invite Zhengliang, too.

122
06:18.070 --> 06:19.950
The president dragged him off.

123
06:26.190 --> 06:27.520
So... just the two of us?

124
06:28.950 --> 06:29.750
Just us two.

125
06:33.930 --> 06:38.040
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

126
06:35.800 --> 06:36.920
I, uh... I need

127
06:36.950 --> 06:38.950
to go home and make dinner for my dad.

128
06:39.680 --> 06:41.280
Then I'll treat you to pizza.

129
06:42.120 --> 06:43.580
Bring your dad along, too.

130
06:51.240 --> 06:56.920
[Accessible Route—Please Keep Clear]

131
06:56.940 --> 07:01.000
[To the Surgical Ward]

132
07:08.000 --> 07:10.330
Uncle Che, you're holding it upside down.

133
07:12.430 --> 07:13.750
You think I'm blind?

134
07:14.270 --> 07:16.130
It's the right way up on this side.

135
07:17.950 --> 07:19.080
Go on, keep looking.

136
07:23.560 --> 07:25.600
This is your second time coming to our place,

137
07:25.600 --> 07:27.040
but you've brought exactly

138
07:27.040 --> 07:28.570
the same things both times.

139
07:29.560 --> 07:30.430
Come clean.

140
07:30.630 --> 07:31.630
Who sent you?

141
07:38.070 --> 07:39.870
Comrade Xiaobo sent me.

142
07:40.000 --> 07:41.720
Got it. Got it.

143
07:42.310 --> 07:43.040
Eat up.

144
07:44.000 --> 07:44.800
Wait a minute.

145
07:47.159 --> 07:49.070
It's not safe to talk here anymore.

146
07:49.070 --> 07:50.070
Let's step aside.

147
07:53.270 --> 07:53.870
Where are you going?

148
07:53.870 --> 07:54.630
Don't ask.

149
07:54.680 --> 07:55.830
Wait, wait.

150
07:57.750 --> 07:59.040
Walls have ears.

151
08:04.240 --> 08:06.640
According to the principles of cosmology,

152
08:06.800 --> 08:08.530
the universe is nearly uniform

153
08:08.720 --> 08:10.510
on sufficiently large scales.

154
08:10.830 --> 08:12.120
The differences in matter density

155
08:12.120 --> 08:13.050
between regions

156
08:13.830 --> 08:15.090
are relatively small.

157
08:15.480 --> 08:17.190
Matter and energy

158
08:17.480 --> 08:18.870
are likely to be distributed homogeneously

159
08:18.870 --> 08:21.720
and isotropically.

160
08:35.120 --> 08:36.510
This is top secret.

161
08:40.669 --> 08:41.960
Top secret.

162
08:42.120 --> 08:43.630
It's a secret between you and me.

163
08:43.630 --> 08:44.670
All right, Uncle Che.

164
08:44.670 --> 08:45.910
No, call me Comrade.

165
08:48.150 --> 08:49.280
All right, Comrade.

166
08:50.960 --> 08:51.670
Mingming,

167
08:53.270 --> 08:55.000
I like this comrade.

168
09:00.200 --> 09:00.960
Comrade.

169
09:03.910 --> 09:04.670
Comrade.

170
09:09.390 --> 09:10.200
Mingming.

171
09:10.600 --> 09:11.270
Mingming.

172
09:11.360 --> 09:12.200
Well,

173
09:12.200 --> 09:14.510
turn right up ahead, and it'll be easier to get a cab there.

174
09:14.510 --> 09:15.370
I'll get going.

175
09:16.720 --> 09:17.910
You've treated me.

176
09:18.480 --> 09:19.320
Let me

177
09:20.480 --> 09:22.080
return the favor.

178
09:24.390 --> 09:25.440
Pick a time.

179
09:30.910 --> 09:32.510
Are you into me or something?

180
09:35.550 --> 09:36.480
What do you mean?

181
09:37.120 --> 09:38.390
We're both adults.

182
09:38.720 --> 09:40.120
Come on, don't play dumb.

183
09:43.750 --> 09:44.440
Yes.

184
09:51.440 --> 09:53.440
I only got divorced a few months ago.

185
09:54.270 --> 09:56.470
And work's been keeping me really busy.

186
09:56.630 --> 09:58.630
I-I also have to apply for a PhD program

187
09:58.630 --> 09:59.890
and take care of my dad.

188
10:00.200 --> 10:03.130
I don't want to get into a new relationship right now.

189
10:05.600 --> 10:07.630
You think I'm not good enough at my job?

190
10:07.630 --> 10:09.430
That I'm not impressive enough?

191
10:13.870 --> 10:15.730
A little, yeah. That's part of it.

192
10:17.840 --> 10:18.630
Right.

193
10:20.910 --> 10:22.120
You're so talented,

194
10:22.960 --> 10:23.960
so hardworking.

195
10:26.120 --> 10:27.360
In your eyes,

196
10:28.120 --> 10:30.000
I must be lazy,

197
10:30.000 --> 10:31.600
just coasting through life,

198
10:32.030 --> 10:33.560
with absolutely no appeal.

199
10:38.200 --> 10:39.000
Got it.

200
10:39.120 --> 10:40.390
Got what?

201
10:44.200 --> 10:45.130
You're so used to

202
10:45.630 --> 10:46.870
being lazy,

203
10:47.600 --> 10:48.670
but deep down,

204
10:48.670 --> 10:50.600
you still want to better yourself.

205
10:50.670 --> 10:52.670
Seeing me rushing around, working hard all day,

206
10:52.670 --> 10:53.720
fills a void

207
10:53.720 --> 10:54.910
in you.

208
10:56.000 --> 10:56.790
Man,

209
10:57.390 --> 10:58.360
take it from me.

210
10:59.200 --> 11:00.510
That's not love.

211
11:01.080 --> 11:04.280
At best, you're looking for what you lack in someone else.

212
11:04.360 --> 11:05.750
What you need to do now

213
11:05.840 --> 11:07.120
is work on yourself.

214
11:07.200 --> 11:08.390
Never pin your hopes

215
11:08.390 --> 11:09.790
on someone else.

216
11:09.960 --> 11:10.750
Got it?

217
11:13.790 --> 11:14.600
Yeah,

218
11:16.480 --> 11:17.480
that makes sense.

219
11:20.670 --> 11:21.730
Thanks for dinner.

220
11:22.510 --> 11:23.510
See you at work.

221
11:25.080 --> 11:26.940
Maybe I am looking for what I lack,

222
11:27.870 --> 11:29.910
but my feelings for you are genuine.

223
11:30.510 --> 11:32.240
Just wait. I'll work on myself,

224
11:32.670 --> 11:34.910
become a better doctor,

225
11:37.200 --> 11:39.130
and then I'll come after you again.

226
12:08.510 --> 12:09.320
I'm off.

227
12:14.790 --> 12:16.050
Why are you still here?

228
12:17.190 --> 12:18.440
I'm gonna play some games.

229
12:18.440 --> 12:19.790
I'll head out after a bit.

230
12:19.790 --> 12:22.440
Done playing?

231
12:22.870 --> 12:23.600
If you're done,

232
12:23.600 --> 12:24.860
walk me home, will you?

233
12:25.960 --> 12:26.790
I'm done.

234
12:27.150 --> 12:27.960
All done.

235
12:28.310 --> 12:32.800
[Traditional Massage by Blind Practitioners]

236
12:28.390 --> 12:29.240
Let's go.

237
12:29.510 --> 12:30.840
Have you changed?

238
12:30.960 --> 12:31.960
I can wait for you.

239
12:31.960 --> 12:32.750
I'm ready.

240
12:33.390 --> 12:34.630
All right, let's go.

241
12:41.870 --> 12:43.200
The tactile paving ends here.

242
12:43.200 --> 12:44.080
Let me help you.

243
12:44.600 --> 12:45.390
No need.

244
12:45.670 --> 12:47.510
I know this stretch like the back of my hand.

245
12:47.510 --> 12:48.670
If I needed help with every little thing,

246
12:48.670 --> 12:50.470
I wouldn't have made it this far.

247
12:51.000 --> 12:52.390
What's wrong with the tactile paving?

248
12:52.390 --> 12:53.790
They did such a shoddy job.

249
12:53.790 --> 12:55.600
How did the city sign off on this construction?

250
12:55.600 --> 12:57.150
It looks good, but it's useless in practice.

251
12:57.150 --> 12:58.790
Well, roads are built

252
12:58.790 --> 13:00.390
to serve the majority, right?

253
13:00.390 --> 13:01.510
We're a minority,

254
13:01.600 --> 13:03.030
so it's only natural that we're overlooked.

255
13:03.030 --> 13:04.390
Before you met me,

256
13:04.390 --> 13:05.390
you probably never even noticed

257
13:05.390 --> 13:05.840
whether there were

258
13:05.840 --> 13:08.640
blind people walking around the streets, did you?

259
13:13.670 --> 13:14.480
I, uh...

260
13:15.320 --> 13:17.580
T-There's something I'd like to ask you,

261
13:17.630 --> 13:19.200
if you don't mind.

262
13:22.240 --> 13:23.550
You want to know why I'm blind,

263
13:23.550 --> 13:24.240
right?

264
13:25.480 --> 13:26.240
Yeah.

265
13:28.670 --> 13:30.870
I wasn't born this way. It was an injury.

266
13:31.550 --> 13:33.750
When I was ten, I was playing downstairs

267
13:33.960 --> 13:35.120
when I ran into this little punk.

268
13:35.120 --> 13:37.150
He sprayed sparks from a lit sparkler into my face.

269
13:37.150 --> 13:38.200
Just my luck.

270
13:39.000 --> 13:41.400
Both my corneas were destroyed on the spot.

271
13:42.870 --> 13:44.030
That's awful.

272
13:44.550 --> 13:45.790
D-Did they catch the kid?

273
13:45.790 --> 13:46.670
They did.

274
13:46.670 --> 13:47.670
But that didn't help.

275
13:47.670 --> 13:49.600
His family was even poorer than mine.

276
13:49.600 --> 13:53.270
They couldn't have paid for the damage, even if they'd sold everything they owned.

277
13:53.270 --> 13:54.270
If you'd gone to a big city,

278
13:54.270 --> 13:56.270
to a major hospital back then,

279
13:56.550 --> 13:57.390
could things have turned out differently?

280
13:57.390 --> 13:58.920
Could it have been treated?

281
13:59.870 --> 14:02.070
There's no point dwelling on what-ifs.

282
14:02.550 --> 14:03.510
Besides,

283
14:04.480 --> 14:05.910
it's been so many years.

284
14:06.550 --> 14:08.880
It's probably too late for treatment now.

285
14:15.630 --> 14:16.200
Careful.

286
14:16.200 --> 14:17.000
Let me move it out of your way

287
14:17.000 --> 14:17.550
before we go.

288
14:17.550 --> 14:18.720
I'm fine, I'm fine.

289
14:18.720 --> 14:19.390
Really,

290
14:19.550 --> 14:20.390
you don't have to.

291
14:20.390 --> 14:21.670
I'm used to this.

292
14:23.790 --> 14:25.240
It's okay. I can manage.

293
14:34.840 --> 14:35.630
Well,

294
14:38.390 --> 14:39.630
if you'd like,

295
14:39.790 --> 14:41.200
I could walk you home every day.

296
14:41.200 --> 14:41.910
That way,

297
14:42.960 --> 14:44.240
you wouldn't

298
14:44.240 --> 14:45.320
have to go through so much on your own.

299
14:45.320 --> 14:46.720
And it'd be safer, right?

300
14:47.440 --> 14:48.240
My dad

301
14:48.360 --> 14:50.870
wanted to pick me up and drop me off every day, too.

302
14:50.870 --> 14:52.600
You know why I wouldn't let him?

303
14:54.440 --> 14:55.240
W-Why?

304
14:55.750 --> 14:57.550
Because one day, he'll grow old.

305
14:58.240 --> 15:00.100
One day, he won't be here anymore.

306
15:01.030 --> 15:02.890
Sooner or later, I'll be on my own.

307
15:07.150 --> 15:08.910
If I learn to live alone now,

308
15:09.600 --> 15:11.730
I won't have to fear anyone leaving me.

309
15:31.630 --> 15:32.510
I'm home.

310
15:34.550 --> 15:35.480
Look over there.

311
15:42.030 --> 15:43.560
On the day I was discharged,

312
15:43.750 --> 15:44.960
I told my dad

313
15:45.910 --> 15:48.170
I'd never wait for someone to come get me.

314
15:48.790 --> 15:50.190
I'd go wherever I wanted,

315
15:50.240 --> 15:51.910
all on my own.

316
15:55.000 --> 15:56.860
I don't have many choices in life,

317
15:57.600 --> 15:59.240
so whenever I do have one,

318
16:00.030 --> 16:01.630
I'll take the initiative.

319
16:02.440 --> 16:04.440
I'll never just sit around and wait.

320
16:10.720 --> 16:11.650
Liu Zhengguang,

321
16:12.320 --> 16:14.180
thanks for walking me home today.

322
16:14.840 --> 16:17.270
But you don't have to do it again.

323
16:57.390 --> 16:58.200
I'm busy.

324
17:09.030 --> 17:09.829
How is it?

325
17:10.480 --> 17:11.829
How am I supposed to tell from just one bite?

326
17:11.829 --> 17:12.589
Give me two more pieces to try.

327
17:12.589 --> 17:13.270
Oh, come on.

328
17:13.270 --> 17:14.480
You're just supposed to check the seasoning.

329
17:14.480 --> 17:15.410
Rainbow Pillar,

330
17:15.960 --> 17:16.640
dinner's ready.

331
17:16.640 --> 17:17.310
Coming!

332
17:17.880 --> 17:19.540
Go get Ai Chen for me, will you?

333
17:21.480 --> 17:22.310
Sure.

334
17:25.640 --> 17:26.750
Sweetheart,

335
17:27.440 --> 17:28.880
dinner's ready!

336
17:29.200 --> 17:29.880
Got it.

337
17:29.880 --> 17:30.610
Come with me.

338
17:35.580 --> 17:39.860
[Crash Course in Literacy: Instructional Talk]

339
17:43.830 --> 17:45.230
The timing's just right.

340
17:45.510 --> 17:46.310
Chen.

341
17:48.270 --> 17:49.070
Zhengguang.

342
17:49.240 --> 17:50.310
Auntie, Uncle.

343
17:51.440 --> 17:52.830
Have you seen Liu Zhengliang?

344
17:52.830 --> 17:53.920
He's not answering his phone,

345
17:53.920 --> 17:54.920
and he's not home.

346
17:55.270 --> 17:56.680
He must be at the hospital.

347
17:56.680 --> 17:57.810
Try calling Junnan.

348
17:58.680 --> 18:00.160
He's already back at work? He just got back!

349
18:00.160 --> 18:01.400
Why not?

350
18:02.310 --> 18:03.970
He's so dedicated to his work.

351
18:04.240 --> 18:05.100
Have you eaten?

352
18:05.110 --> 18:06.200
Come join us.

353
18:06.240 --> 18:06.920
No, thanks, Auntie.

354
18:06.920 --> 18:07.720
I'm not hungry.

355
18:07.720 --> 18:08.580
I'll get going.

356
18:09.030 --> 18:09.830
Don't go!

357
18:11.920 --> 18:13.650
Your Auntie Si made dumplings.

358
18:35.110 --> 18:36.170
Is there any for me?

359
18:46.350 --> 18:47.310
What is it?

360
18:47.510 --> 18:48.960
What do you mean, what is it?

361
18:48.960 --> 18:50.070
You seem a little down,

362
18:50.070 --> 18:50.720
with that long face.

363
18:50.720 --> 18:51.920
Just checking on you.

364
18:52.880 --> 18:54.510
Seriously, can you go back to your usual self?

365
18:54.510 --> 18:55.720
I'm not used to this.

366
19:02.200 --> 19:03.030
Remember

367
19:04.590 --> 19:06.270
what Mom said one Dragon Boat Festival?

368
19:06.270 --> 19:07.200
Something

369
19:07.550 --> 19:08.720
about dumplings.

370
19:10.240 --> 19:11.030
Yeah.

371
19:12.160 --> 19:12.960
She said

372
19:13.270 --> 19:15.240
she'd learn to make dumplings herself.

373
19:15.240 --> 19:16.590
And from then on,

374
19:16.590 --> 19:18.270
the dumplings every year were especially good.

375
19:18.270 --> 19:19.400
That's not the line.

376
19:24.880 --> 19:25.680
She said

377
19:26.590 --> 19:27.400
that since I came home

378
19:27.400 --> 19:29.000
only in the summer each year,

379
19:29.270 --> 19:30.070
the Dragon Boat Festival

380
19:30.070 --> 19:32.000
was our family's Spring Festival.

381
19:32.030 --> 19:34.510
And you have to eat dumplings at Spring Festival,

382
19:34.510 --> 19:35.310
right?

383
19:38.880 --> 19:39.680
You actually remember that.

384
19:39.680 --> 19:41.030
Of course I do.

385
19:41.160 --> 19:42.240
It's not like I don't have a heart.

386
19:42.240 --> 19:42.880
Then why do you act

387
19:42.880 --> 19:44.400
like you don't?

388
19:47.790 --> 19:48.590
Fine,

389
19:49.680 --> 19:50.940
I'll stop pretending.

390
19:51.270 --> 19:52.550
You've seen right through me.

391
19:52.550 --> 19:53.440
I am human.

392
19:56.030 --> 19:57.090
Round of applause.

393
19:57.790 --> 19:59.160
Congratulations on realizing

394
19:59.160 --> 20:00.160
you're human.

395
20:00.550 --> 20:01.550
How would you like me to play along?

396
20:01.550 --> 20:02.720
Should I... should I celebrate with you?

397
20:02.720 --> 20:04.440
Hooray! My brother is human!

398
20:04.830 --> 20:05.680
Hooray!

399
20:11.110 --> 20:11.840
Zhengguang.

400
20:12.550 --> 20:14.350
It's been so long since you last called me big brother.

401
20:14.350 --> 20:15.160
Really?

402
20:15.240 --> 20:17.000
I... I didn't even realize.

403
20:20.480 --> 20:21.720
Have some while they're still hot.

404
20:21.720 --> 20:22.590
They're delicious.

405
20:22.590 --> 20:24.120
They taste just like Mom's.

406
20:24.750 --> 20:25.920
You know why?

407
20:27.270 --> 20:28.070
Why?

408
20:28.720 --> 20:31.000
Because Mom never actually learned to make them.

409
20:31.000 --> 20:31.720
Every year,

410
20:31.720 --> 20:32.790
she'd get them from Aunt Mi Si,

411
20:32.790 --> 20:33.880
then tell you

412
20:33.880 --> 20:35.280
she'd made them herself.

413
20:41.480 --> 20:42.160
Guess I didn't know

414
20:42.160 --> 20:43.270
Mom as well as I thought.

415
20:43.270 --> 20:44.000
Same here.

416
20:44.400 --> 20:45.590
I didn't know Dad either.

417
20:45.590 --> 20:47.120
I never even got to meet him.

418
20:49.480 --> 20:50.750
My memories of him

419
20:51.270 --> 20:52.530
are pretty vague, too.

420
20:53.070 --> 20:54.670
Not much clearer than yours.

421
21:08.880 --> 21:09.610
Zhengliang,

422
21:10.400 --> 21:11.350
I miss her.

423
21:12.590 --> 21:13.400
I mean, Mom.

424
21:15.720 --> 21:16.510
Me too.

425
21:24.440 --> 21:26.710
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

426
21:25.640 --> 21:26.920
It's the third day after surgery.

427
21:26.920 --> 21:28.720
The patient is fully conscious.

428
21:29.310 --> 21:30.240
His Glasgow Coma Scale score

429
21:30.240 --> 21:31.350
is 14,

430
21:32.070 --> 21:34.240
so he can communicate without much difficulty.

431
21:34.240 --> 21:34.880
He reports

432
21:34.880 --> 21:36.440
mild pain at the wound site,

433
21:36.920 --> 21:38.920
with no nausea or vomiting.

434
21:40.160 --> 21:41.790
-Who's that? -The patient's vital signs are stable.

435
21:41.790 --> 21:44.190
-His ex-wife. -His temperature is 36.8 °C.

436
21:44.310 --> 21:45.110
Good.

437
21:45.200 --> 21:47.260
Movement in all four limbs is normal.

438
21:47.400 --> 21:49.270
Left-sided muscle strength

439
21:49.350 --> 21:51.000
has improved to 4+.

440
21:51.270 --> 21:53.440
His latest blood count and electrolyte levels

441
21:53.440 --> 21:55.100
are all within normal ranges.

442
22:05.070 --> 22:06.240
Dr. Che has already explained

443
22:06.240 --> 22:07.840
his condition to you, right?

444
22:09.030 --> 22:10.070
The surgery to treat his injuries

445
22:10.070 --> 22:10.930
went very well.

446
22:11.070 --> 22:13.270
We also successfully removed the hematoma

447
22:13.270 --> 22:15.110
and the remaining foreign objects.

448
22:15.110 --> 22:15.680
But

449
22:15.680 --> 22:17.030
his preoperative CT scan

450
22:17.030 --> 22:19.490
suggested an abnormality inside his skull.

451
22:20.550 --> 22:21.510
Postoperative MRI

452
22:21.510 --> 22:23.700
and pathology results confirmed

453
22:23.830 --> 22:25.440
that he has a malignant tumor

454
22:25.830 --> 22:28.270
in his right temporal lobe.

455
22:30.070 --> 22:31.960
I believe this may well be

456
22:32.350 --> 22:34.640
why his personality changed so drastically.

457
22:34.640 --> 22:35.350
So he'll need

458
22:35.350 --> 22:37.880
another operation

459
22:37.880 --> 22:39.440
to remove the tumor.

460
22:41.200 --> 22:42.680
Of course, not right away.

461
22:42.960 --> 22:43.350
Once his surgical wound

462
22:43.350 --> 22:45.030
has healed,

463
22:46.110 --> 22:47.680
we can plan to proceed with the operation

464
22:47.680 --> 22:48.920
as soon as possible.

465
22:49.110 --> 22:51.910
Otherwise, it could shorten his life expectancy.

466
22:59.590 --> 23:01.390
But I don't have much money left.

467
23:02.200 --> 23:03.110
The money I paid before

468
23:03.110 --> 23:04.310
was all borrowed.

469
23:05.350 --> 23:06.830
No matter how much more I scrape together,

470
23:06.830 --> 23:09.360
I can only manage ten or twenty thousand yuan.

471
23:09.400 --> 23:11.030
What if that's not enough

472
23:11.880 --> 23:13.210
for another operation?

473
23:14.680 --> 23:15.550
Doesn't he

474
23:16.160 --> 23:17.640
have any other family?

475
23:18.720 --> 23:19.510
No.

476
23:20.400 --> 23:21.830
We have a child together.

477
23:22.400 --> 23:23.330
Three years old.

478
23:24.110 --> 23:25.910
The child usually lives with me.

479
23:26.830 --> 23:28.680
How long have you been divorced?

480
23:30.030 --> 23:31.070
Less than a year.

481
23:37.830 --> 23:38.790
I understand.

482
23:38.960 --> 23:39.920
If you have any reservations

483
23:39.920 --> 23:41.070
about the surgery,

484
23:41.350 --> 23:42.200
or...

485
23:45.920 --> 23:47.920
if you don't want to take responsibility for him anymore,

486
23:47.920 --> 23:49.320
you can tell me directly.

487
23:57.920 --> 23:58.880
Actually,

488
24:00.480 --> 24:02.310
he used to be such a kind person,

489
24:02.590 --> 24:04.320
and he had a really good temper.

490
24:06.830 --> 24:09.350
Then he started getting more and more irritable.

491
24:09.350 --> 24:10.550
I kept wondering

492
24:10.790 --> 24:12.190
why he'd changed so much.

493
24:14.270 --> 24:15.640
Turns out he was sick.

494
24:17.550 --> 24:18.680
No wonder

495
24:18.680 --> 24:21.280
he'd be fine one moment and irritable the next.

496
24:28.160 --> 24:30.360
He was the one who asked for the divorce.

497
24:30.790 --> 24:33.120
He brought it up as soon as he was admitted.

498
24:36.960 --> 24:38.030
He just didn't want

499
24:38.030 --> 24:40.240
to drag me and our child down, did he?

500
24:44.350 --> 24:45.400
Dr. Liu,

501
24:46.000 --> 24:48.530
could you please think of some way to save him?

502
24:49.790 --> 24:51.270
He's a good man.

503
24:55.920 --> 24:57.880
He really is.

504
25:03.110 --> 25:03.880
President,

505
25:04.070 --> 25:05.480
didn't you say

506
25:05.720 --> 25:07.920
Du Fang could be a good publicity angle?

507
25:07.920 --> 25:09.030
Here we go again.

508
25:09.880 --> 25:11.480
Zhang Jiao only got a partial waiver.

509
25:11.480 --> 25:13.030
You want this one completely free?

510
25:13.030 --> 25:14.830
You can't expect everything to go your way.

511
25:14.830 --> 25:16.230
This isn't a charity.

512
25:18.030 --> 25:20.240
You were the one who sent me to do the interview, right?

513
25:20.240 --> 25:21.030
I did it.

514
25:21.030 --> 25:21.920
And now you're telling me

515
25:21.920 --> 25:22.980
to just let him die?

516
25:23.070 --> 25:24.400
Won't that end up becoming

517
25:24.400 --> 25:26.030
a case of medical malpractice?

518
25:26.030 --> 25:29.030
Xiaoximen Hospital is on the verge of being shut down.

519
25:29.030 --> 25:30.830
I'm just trying to keep it alive.

520
25:31.310 --> 25:32.030
Dr. Liu,

521
25:32.680 --> 25:35.030
there are plenty of people in this world who can't afford medical care.

522
25:35.030 --> 25:37.030
I've already done everything I can.

523
25:39.350 --> 25:40.830
Then why don't you sign off on it first?

524
25:40.000 --> 25:43.620
[Decision-Making Procedure for "Three Major and One Important" Matters]

525
25:41.400 --> 25:42.960
We can put his medical bills on hold for now.

526
25:42.960 --> 25:44.640
The hospital's going under anyway.

527
25:44.640 --> 25:46.640
What's one more unpaid bill, right?

528
25:48.350 --> 25:49.720
Y-You can't keep milking the same target

529
25:49.720 --> 25:51.790
over and over.

530
25:53.590 --> 25:55.050
President, let me do this.

531
25:55.310 --> 25:55.830
Let me.

532
25:56.750 --> 26:00.130
[Decision-Making Procedure for "Three Major and One Important" Matters]

533
25:59.680 --> 26:00.350
President,

534
26:00.550 --> 26:02.610
could you please think of something?

535
26:02.920 --> 26:04.240
You're resourceful.

536
26:04.400 --> 26:06.260
I'm sure you'll find a way, right?

537
26:06.830 --> 26:07.590
I promise

538
26:08.350 --> 26:09.880
this will be the last time.

539
26:10.510 --> 26:11.310
Please?

540
26:12.070 --> 26:13.240
Oh, give me a break.

541
26:22.350 --> 26:22.920
Anyway,

542
26:22.920 --> 26:24.070
I saw you last time.

543
26:24.160 --> 26:25.240
You were secretly watching

544
26:25.240 --> 26:26.350
girl group dance videos in your office.

545
26:26.350 --> 26:27.110
That won't work.

546
26:27.110 --> 26:28.240
Not a chance.

547
26:30.750 --> 26:33.810
You snuck in and watched for ages yourself, didn't you?

548
26:43.110 --> 26:44.770
Before I came back to Fucheng,

549
26:45.310 --> 26:46.110
I met a patient

550
26:46.110 --> 26:47.680
with high-grade glioma.

551
26:49.240 --> 26:51.040
He was even younger than Du Fang,

552
26:51.240 --> 26:54.170
but there was nothing we could do but wait for the end.

553
26:56.590 --> 26:58.590
There was nothing I could do for him.

554
26:58.920 --> 27:00.920
But this patient still has a chance.

555
27:03.030 --> 27:04.290
Please, think it over.

556
27:05.240 --> 27:07.640
Tens of thousands of yuan could save a life.

557
27:07.880 --> 27:08.640
And he's dealing with

558
27:08.640 --> 27:11.240
both a gunshot wound and a temporal lobe tumor.

559
27:40.830 --> 27:42.160
Now that you mention it,

560
27:43.400 --> 27:44.830
there might be a way.

561
27:48.160 --> 27:49.000
But you'll have to give up

562
27:49.000 --> 27:50.550
control over his treatment.

563
27:50.550 --> 27:51.830
As long as we can save his life,

564
27:51.830 --> 27:53.690
I don't care about anything else.

565
28:07.020 --> 28:10.770
[Massage Clinic Run by Blind Practitioners]

566
28:08.000 --> 28:08.830
Take care.

567
28:13.830 --> 28:14.550
Jia,

568
28:15.240 --> 28:16.440
what brings you here?

569
28:18.750 --> 28:19.830
I asked him to come.

570
28:34.160 --> 28:35.200
The Taoist asked,

571
28:35.400 --> 28:37.030
"Was General Yang Zaixing

572
28:37.030 --> 28:39.350
your ancestor?"

573
28:39.790 --> 28:43.190
Yang Tiexin replied, "He was my great-great-grandfather."

574
28:43.270 --> 28:44.400
The next part goes…

575
28:44.920 --> 28:47.750
The Taoist immediately showed his respect

576
28:47.830 --> 28:49.400
and clasped his hands in greeting.

577
28:49.400 --> 28:52.440
"I mistook you two for villains just now.

578
28:52.590 --> 28:54.120
Please forgive my offense.

579
28:54.310 --> 28:57.240
I see now that you are descendants of a loyal and honorable family.

580
28:57.240 --> 28:58.720
I sincerely apologize.

581
28:59.440 --> 29:01.680
May I ask your esteemed name?"

582
29:08.240 --> 29:09.640
Why did you stop reading?

583
29:13.510 --> 29:14.310
Well,

584
29:14.920 --> 29:16.720
I'd never imagined

585
29:16.720 --> 29:18.780
anyone would think I had a nice voice.

586
29:20.790 --> 29:22.070
When we first met,

587
29:22.070 --> 29:23.930
you even said I was good-looking.

588
29:24.880 --> 29:26.270
It was the first time anyone

589
29:26.270 --> 29:28.070
had ever said that about me, too.

590
29:29.920 --> 29:31.320
You heard that part, too.

591
29:33.310 --> 29:34.880
Am I your type?

592
29:39.790 --> 29:40.720
I'm teasing you.

593
29:41.480 --> 29:42.550
Go on reading.

594
29:47.550 --> 29:49.000
Guo Xiaotian said,

595
29:49.000 --> 29:50.590
"Think nothing of it!

596
29:50.590 --> 29:52.440
Please, come inside, Taoist priest,

597
29:52.440 --> 29:54.240
and join us for three more cups."

598
29:54.350 --> 29:56.640
At this point, Yang Tiexin and Guo Xiaotian

599
29:56.640 --> 29:57.900
felt a little awkward,

600
29:58.070 --> 29:58.640
you know?

601
29:58.640 --> 30:00.300
They'd just beaten the man up.

602
30:00.310 --> 30:01.310
And the Taoist priest

603
30:01.310 --> 30:03.310
wasn't one to hold a grudge.

604
30:04.030 --> 30:05.400
As he picked up his spear,

605
30:05.400 --> 30:06.440
the Taoist priest said,

606
30:06.440 --> 30:07.170
"Excellent!

607
30:07.440 --> 30:10.680
I was just hoping to have a good drink with you two!"

608
30:20.370 --> 30:22.780
[Starry Night]

609
30:29.680 --> 30:32.550
♪ You belong to me ♪

610
30:32.980 --> 30:34.570
♪ I belong to— ♪

611
30:33.680 --> 30:34.680
Everyone's here.

612
30:34.790 --> 30:36.350
So, Huang, are you done with your handover?

613
30:36.350 --> 30:37.310
All done. I'm off work.

614
30:37.310 --> 30:39.350
Yang got here early. He's already handed over.

615
30:39.350 --> 30:40.160
Well,

616
30:40.270 --> 30:41.070
um,

617
30:41.880 --> 30:43.680
after things settle down a bit,

618
30:44.030 --> 30:45.480
I'd like to treat everyone

619
30:45.480 --> 30:46.550
to a meal.

620
30:47.200 --> 30:48.330
You're treating us?

621
30:48.550 --> 30:49.350
What for?

622
30:50.000 --> 30:51.310
W-Well, I left,

623
30:51.310 --> 30:52.480
but now I'm back.

624
30:52.720 --> 30:53.400
I've caused everyone

625
30:53.400 --> 30:54.930
a lot of trouble, haven't I?

626
30:55.640 --> 30:56.030
So,

627
30:56.310 --> 30:57.310
j-just a small gathering.

628
30:57.310 --> 30:58.160
A small one.

629
30:58.160 --> 30:58.830
Just the few of us

630
30:58.830 --> 30:59.760
from the office,

631
30:59.790 --> 31:02.030
plus Ai Chen and my younger brother.

632
31:04.720 --> 31:05.470
Dr. Liu.

633
31:05.510 --> 31:07.440
I-I have to give you a hug.

634
31:08.400 --> 31:09.480
J-Just let me know

635
31:09.480 --> 31:10.480
the date in advance.

636
31:10.480 --> 31:11.790
I'll have Li reserve a large private room.

637
31:11.790 --> 31:12.440
No need,

638
31:12.480 --> 31:13.110
Huang.

639
31:13.160 --> 31:15.360
I'll take care of everything this time.

640
31:15.880 --> 31:18.110
You're really on top of everything now, huh?

641
31:18.110 --> 31:19.310
Absolutely perfect.

642
31:19.480 --> 31:19.960
All right,

643
31:19.960 --> 31:20.960
I'll wait to hear from you.

644
31:20.960 --> 31:21.640
See you.

645
31:21.750 --> 31:22.440
-I'm off. -Bye-bye. Bye-bye.

646
31:22.440 --> 31:23.110
I'm heading out first.

647
31:23.110 --> 31:23.880
Look at you, Zhengliang.

648
31:23.880 --> 31:24.920
You're making progress!

649
31:24.920 --> 31:26.980
I've been looking forward to it, too.

650
31:27.000 --> 31:28.660
Anyway, I'd better get going.

651
31:30.590 --> 31:31.240
Bye-bye.

652
31:33.400 --> 31:34.800
Am I really that perfect?

653
31:46.400 --> 31:47.460
What are you doing?

654
31:50.270 --> 31:52.000
I didn't sleep well last night.

655
31:52.350 --> 31:53.410
I'm a little tired.

656
31:54.400 --> 31:55.530
I'm getting sleepy.

657
31:58.110 --> 31:59.240
Have you guys heard?

658
31:59.350 --> 32:00.830
Our hospital's shutting down.

659
31:59.770 --> 32:09.500
[Triage Desk]

660
32:01.070 --> 32:01.960
Wasn't that just a rumor?

661
32:01.960 --> 32:03.760
Director Li denied it last week.

662
32:03.830 --> 32:05.270
And you just believe him?

663
32:05.350 --> 32:06.240
I heard

664
32:06.350 --> 32:08.550
it's definitely closing within 2 months.

665
32:08.550 --> 32:09.270
What?

666
32:09.270 --> 32:11.350
Then what are we supposed to do about our jobs?

667
32:09.550 --> 32:17.000
[Hospital Oversight and Complaints Hotline]

668
32:11.790 --> 32:12.920
Apparently,

669
32:12.920 --> 32:14.030
about one in ten of us

670
32:14.030 --> 32:15.240
can transfer to No. 6 Hospital.

671
32:15.240 --> 32:16.790
And the rest will be laid off?

672
32:16.790 --> 32:17.640
Ying,

673
32:17.000 --> 32:21.930
[Patient Satisfaction Survey]

674
32:17.680 --> 32:19.000
are you sure about this?

675
32:19.000 --> 32:20.130
I'm almost certain.

676
32:20.240 --> 32:20.920
Dr. Chen's here.

677
32:20.920 --> 32:21.750
Dr. Chen, come here.

678
32:21.750 --> 32:22.480
Well...

679
32:22.010 --> 32:28.480
[No smoking]

680
32:22.590 --> 32:23.400
Junnan,

681
32:23.550 --> 32:25.680
is our hospital really shutting down?

682
32:25.790 --> 32:27.000
So what if it is?

683
32:27.270 --> 32:28.600
We can all stop working.

684
32:28.830 --> 32:30.030
Then we won't have to see each other anymore. Sounds great to me.

685
32:30.030 --> 32:32.030
Oh, it's over. It's 100% confirmed.

686
32:57.750 --> 32:58.350
Morning.

687
33:09.310 --> 33:10.540
I'll go buy some.

688
33:11.270 --> 33:12.000
Give it to me.

689
33:18.790 --> 33:20.190
There's still some left.

690
33:21.110 --> 33:22.710
You're pretty resourceful.

691
33:22.720 --> 33:24.720
I'll buy some on my way back tonight.

692
33:35.720 --> 33:36.650
Liu Zhengliang,

693
33:38.070 --> 33:39.800
do you think I have a nice voice?

694
33:46.030 --> 33:46.830
It's not bad,

695
33:47.440 --> 33:48.840
but it's not good either.

696
33:50.640 --> 33:51.440
Why?

697
33:51.590 --> 33:52.920
You want to be a host?

698
33:53.960 --> 33:55.090
I want to be a singer.

699
33:58.920 --> 33:59.640
Liu Zhengguang,

700
33:59.640 --> 34:00.920
stop making me laugh.

701
34:01.350 --> 34:02.030
If you can sing,

702
34:02.030 --> 34:03.240
then pigs can fly.

703
34:03.790 --> 34:05.640
I was obviously talking nonsense,

704
34:05.640 --> 34:07.700
but you just had to keep picking on me.

705
34:08.630 --> 34:10.320
Sorry. Reflex.

706
34:15.710 --> 34:16.510
Zhengguang,

707
34:19.840 --> 34:21.840
whatever you want to do in the future,

708
34:21.840 --> 34:22.960
I'll support you.

709
34:24.000 --> 34:25.730
Because I'm your only brother.

710
34:34.070 --> 34:35.000
You know,

711
34:35.440 --> 34:37.110
maybe you should go back to being yourself.

712
34:37.110 --> 34:38.909
You really don't have to do this.

713
34:39.030 --> 34:40.830
You're fine just the way you are.

714
34:41.030 --> 34:42.030
No way.

715
34:42.550 --> 34:43.320
I've already said I'd do it,

716
34:43.320 --> 34:44.650
so I have to keep my word.

717
34:47.190 --> 34:48.440
Could you not say that

718
34:48.440 --> 34:49.510
while I'm brushing my teeth?

719
34:49.510 --> 34:50.480
It's making me sick.

720
34:50.480 --> 34:51.840
Is your stomach upset?

721
34:52.190 --> 34:53.989
Want me to get you some medicine?

722
34:54.630 --> 34:55.840
I'm kidding.

723
35:02.030 --> 35:03.070
So am I.

724
35:10.150 --> 35:10.960
Sweetheart,

725
35:11.590 --> 35:12.800
what's wrong?

726
35:13.320 --> 35:15.190
D-Do you need to go to the hospital?

727
35:15.190 --> 35:16.150
No, no.

728
35:18.070 --> 35:20.800
Did you eat something that didn't agree with you?

729
35:20.960 --> 35:22.150
It's not that.

730
35:22.880 --> 35:25.280
This has happened before.

731
35:44.400 --> 35:45.070
I'm fine.

732
35:45.070 --> 35:47.270
Maybe the cold air irritated my throat.

733
36:05.710 --> 36:07.760
Look at you! You've thrown up,

734
36:09.150 --> 36:10.480
and your face is so pale.

735
36:10.960 --> 36:11.760
It's fine.

736
36:11.960 --> 36:15.090
Here, drink some water. It'll help settle your stomach.

737
36:16.630 --> 36:17.630
I feel better.

738
36:25.430 --> 36:27.680
[Crash Course in Literacy: Instructional Talk]

739
36:28.550 --> 36:30.810
Did Liu Zhengliang say something to you?

740
36:32.670 --> 36:34.000
I just wanted to try learning on my own.

741
36:34.000 --> 36:34.800
No way.

742
36:35.510 --> 36:37.670
You've tried learning before, remember?

743
36:37.670 --> 36:39.800
You were throwing up so badly you almost brought up bile.

744
36:39.800 --> 36:41.550
You swore you'd never study again.

745
36:41.550 --> 36:42.400
Over the years,

746
36:42.400 --> 36:43.320
you've gotten more and more

747
36:43.320 --> 36:44.780
used to being illiterate.

748
36:44.880 --> 36:46.030
Why would you suddenly

749
36:46.030 --> 36:47.960
want to learn again after one trip out?

750
36:47.960 --> 36:49.420
It must be Liu Zhengliang.

751
36:50.510 --> 36:51.440
I'm telling you,

752
36:52.510 --> 36:53.920
if he looks down on you,

753
36:54.630 --> 36:56.560
you absolutely cannot be with him.

754
36:57.110 --> 36:57.960
Understand?

755
37:02.920 --> 37:04.800
I really did want to try on my own.

756
37:13.550 --> 37:15.960
I haven't really gone anywhere in all these years.

757
37:15.960 --> 37:17.320
I was scared, you know.

758
37:20.070 --> 37:22.150
And I couldn't be bothered

759
37:22.150 --> 37:24.210
to explain everything to strangers.

760
37:25.190 --> 37:26.510
But on this trip,

761
37:26.510 --> 37:28.320
I found something that works pretty well:

762
37:28.320 --> 37:29.980
pretending to be a foreigner.

763
37:30.630 --> 37:31.760
Oh no...

764
37:32.750 --> 37:33.550
What do I do?

765
37:37.590 --> 37:39.450
Which line am I supposed to get in?

766
37:46.820 --> 37:47.690
Hello.

767
37:47.800 --> 37:48.400
Hello.

768
37:49.760 --> 37:51.230
This, this...

769
37:51.710 --> 37:53.910
I can't understand a single thing here.

770
37:54.840 --> 37:56.110
It's pretty convincing.

771
37:56.110 --> 37:56.840
Really.

772
37:59.590 --> 38:00.400
But

773
38:02.840 --> 38:04.230
I've been thinking,

774
38:07.280 --> 38:09.740
I can't go on like this for the rest of my life,

775
38:09.920 --> 38:10.710
can I?

776
38:16.440 --> 38:17.710
I want to be able to read

777
38:17.710 --> 38:19.440
what's on my boarding pass.

778
38:23.710 --> 38:25.480
And I want to understand

779
38:27.280 --> 38:28.230
what's written

780
38:28.230 --> 38:29.890
on those delivery boxes, too.

781
38:31.030 --> 38:32.920
When people text me,

782
38:33.320 --> 38:34.150
I want to be able to text them

783
38:34.150 --> 38:35.440
back and forth,

784
38:35.440 --> 38:36.190
you know?

785
38:36.230 --> 38:38.000
Share what's really on my mind.

786
38:43.070 --> 38:44.400
So Liu Zhengliang

787
38:44.510 --> 38:46.970
never rubbed my illiteracy in my face at all.

788
38:49.030 --> 38:51.400
If anything, I feel like his coming back

789
38:51.400 --> 38:52.840
has inspired me.

790
38:53.960 --> 38:56.290
His condition was more serious than mine.

791
38:56.760 --> 38:57.760
He's still willing to try.

792
38:57.760 --> 38:58.920
So why can't I?

793
39:06.000 --> 39:06.800
President.

794
39:06.200 --> 39:10.160
[Healing pain with compassion, lighting up hope with dedication]

795
39:07.150 --> 39:08.000
You're here.

796
39:08.710 --> 39:10.570
Let me introduce everyone to you.

797
39:11.320 --> 39:12.520
Chief Physician Qin,

798
39:13.000 --> 39:14.190
a neurosurgeon

799
39:14.480 --> 39:15.610
from No. 1 Hospital.

800
39:15.800 --> 39:16.230
Hello.

801
39:16.280 --> 39:17.000
Hello.

802
39:17.000 --> 39:17.920
Chief Physician Qin

803
39:17.920 --> 39:19.320
is the top neurosurgeon

804
39:20.150 --> 39:21.840
in Fucheng.

805
39:22.000 --> 39:23.440
You're too kind.

806
39:23.440 --> 39:24.480
Everyone here is part

807
39:24.480 --> 39:26.210
of Chief Physician Qin's team.

808
39:26.360 --> 39:27.690
They're all top-notch.

809
39:28.230 --> 39:29.890
All right, let's get started.

810
39:30.480 --> 39:32.280
Associate Chief Physician Liu

811
39:32.280 --> 39:33.400
certainly has an air of authority.

812
39:33.400 --> 39:34.090
You can tell he's the one

813
39:34.090 --> 39:35.380
who gives the orders.

814
39:38.000 --> 39:38.800
And you are?

815
39:39.070 --> 39:40.470
My name is Ye Zhengqiang.

816
39:43.630 --> 39:44.590
I was just organizing some documents,

817
39:44.590 --> 39:45.590
so I'm a little late.

818
39:45.590 --> 39:46.550
some documents.

819
39:46.920 --> 39:48.320
Let me introduce myself.

820
39:48.400 --> 39:49.670
I'm Liu Zhengliang,

821
39:49.800 --> 39:51.190
an ordinary doctor

822
39:51.190 --> 39:52.520
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

823
39:53.070 --> 39:54.000
Thank you all

824
39:54.000 --> 39:55.730
for stepping in to help Du Fang.

825
39:57.000 --> 39:58.230
As long as you cover

826
39:58.230 --> 39:59.630
all of Du Fang's medical expenses

827
39:59.630 --> 40:00.710
this time,

828
40:02.550 --> 40:03.960
we'll even have our President Long

829
40:03.960 --> 40:05.070
get onto the table and dance for you

830
40:05.070 --> 40:06.990
or perform a sing-and-dance duet Whatever you like.

831
40:06.990 --> 40:15.350
[Healing pain with compassion, lighting up hope with dedication]

832
40:07.320 --> 40:09.190
Who'd want to see President Long dance?

833
40:09.190 --> 40:10.800
Well, I can dance if needed.

834
40:10.920 --> 40:11.920
I wanna see. I wanna see.

835
40:11.920 --> 40:12.670
You...

836
40:13.480 --> 40:15.940
Look how supportive Chief Physician Qin is!

837
40:16.070 --> 40:17.920
All right, enough joking around.

838
40:17.920 --> 40:19.450
Let me say a few words first.

839
40:19.800 --> 40:21.800
Du Fang's case

840
40:21.840 --> 40:23.070
is rather unusual.

841
40:23.550 --> 40:24.840
He's agreed

842
40:24.840 --> 40:26.070
to join our team's

843
40:26.070 --> 40:27.630
clinical trial

844
40:27.630 --> 40:29.070
for temporal lobe tumors

845
40:29.320 --> 40:30.070
and has signed

846
40:30.070 --> 40:31.600
the informed consent form.

847
40:33.070 --> 40:35.630
The treatment costs

848
40:35.630 --> 40:36.920
will be covered

849
40:36.920 --> 40:38.880
by our department's research funds.

850
40:38.880 --> 40:40.920
All research findings from this case

851
40:40.920 --> 40:43.400
will be owned

852
40:43.440 --> 40:44.280
by the neurosurgery team

853
40:44.280 --> 40:46.000
at No. 1 Hospital.

854
40:48.480 --> 40:49.410
President Long,

855
40:49.670 --> 40:50.880
does your hospital

856
40:50.880 --> 40:52.710
have any objections?

857
40:53.000 --> 40:53.880
None from me.

858
40:57.280 --> 40:58.110
Me neither.

859
40:58.360 --> 41:00.550
Sounds good. We'll go with what President says.

860
41:00.550 --> 41:01.590
Then let's

861
41:02.070 --> 41:03.550
discuss the surgical plan.

862
41:03.550 --> 41:04.410
Enlarge the...

863
41:05.340 --> 41:07.940
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

864
41:08.060 --> 41:12.490
[Non-Smoking Ward] [Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

865
41:13.190 --> 41:14.480
I'm not dead yet,

866
41:15.550 --> 41:17.400
and you're flirting with other people without even bothering to hide it?

867
41:17.260 --> 41:23.010
[Non-Smoking Ward] [Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

868
41:17.670 --> 41:19.200
What are you talking about?

869
41:19.480 --> 41:20.880
I'm just picking up odd jobs

870
41:20.880 --> 41:22.230
in the group chat to make some money.

871
41:22.230 --> 41:23.920
Otherwise, my kid and I would've starved to death by now.

872
41:23.110 --> 41:28.290
[Ward 12]

873
41:23.920 --> 41:24.510
Right.

874
41:24.880 --> 41:26.810
I'm keeping you from making money.

875
41:28.000 --> 41:28.800
Get out.

876
41:28.880 --> 41:29.590
What's with that attitude?

877
41:29.590 --> 41:31.550
Can you just get out already? Just leave!

878
41:31.550 --> 41:32.750
What's going on here?

879
41:35.550 --> 41:36.280
Temporal lobe tumors can indeed

880
41:36.280 --> 41:38.000
cause psychiatric symptoms.

881
41:38.400 --> 41:39.800
We'd considered

882
41:39.920 --> 41:40.880
that possibility before,

883
41:40.880 --> 41:41.550
but we didn't expect

884
41:41.550 --> 41:43.280
the symptoms to be this severe.

885
41:43.760 --> 41:45.710
He still needs surgery.

886
41:46.400 --> 41:48.330
What surgery? Another operation?

887
41:49.920 --> 41:51.440
Better to die sooner and be done with it.

888
41:51.440 --> 41:53.640
How can you talk to the doctor like that?

889
41:54.800 --> 41:56.190
I'm sorry, Dr. Liu.

890
41:56.480 --> 41:57.710
Please don't take it to heart.

891
41:57.710 --> 41:58.230
It's okay.

892
41:58.230 --> 42:00.430
Look at you, acting all high and mighty.

893
42:00.550 --> 42:02.400
You're the only good person here, right?

894
42:02.400 --> 42:03.880
What are you trying to do?

895
42:03.960 --> 42:05.510
It's okay, it's okay.

896
42:06.070 --> 42:07.000
If you need anything,

897
42:07.000 --> 42:08.510
just ask the nurse on duty.

898
42:09.320 --> 42:10.400
Thank you, Doctor.

899
42:10.800 --> 42:12.530
What are you thanking them for?

900
42:13.110 --> 42:14.640
Didn't I tell you to get out?

901
42:18.230 --> 42:19.110
Get out!

902
42:21.030 --> 42:21.800
Get out!

903
42:33.670 --> 42:35.400
Du Fang's irritability

904
42:35.400 --> 42:36.550
is getting worse.

905
42:37.070 --> 42:38.470
The best course of action

906
42:38.480 --> 42:40.680
is still to operate as soon as possible.

907
42:40.710 --> 42:41.800
I feel so bad

908
42:41.800 --> 42:43.070
for his ex-wife.

909
42:43.400 --> 42:44.670
She has to take care of their child

910
42:44.670 --> 42:46.600
and look after him at the same time.

911
42:46.760 --> 42:48.420
And with him acting like this,

912
42:48.440 --> 42:49.150
it's more than most people

913
42:49.150 --> 42:50.360
could handle.

914
42:51.590 --> 42:52.190
I think

915
42:52.190 --> 42:53.920
she's close to breaking point.

916
42:55.480 --> 42:56.190
-President. -President.

917
42:56.190 --> 42:57.480
I've been looking for you.

918
42:57.480 --> 42:59.070
Chief Physician Qin just called.

919
42:59.070 --> 42:59.960
She said you're

920
42:59.960 --> 43:01.280
going to perform Du Fang's surgery.

921
43:01.280 --> 43:02.400
She'll oversee the operation,

922
43:02.400 --> 43:04.600
and her team will provide full support.

923
43:05.590 --> 43:07.710
Wasn't Dr. Ye supposed to do it?

924
43:08.110 --> 43:09.440
Ye Zhengqiang injured his hand

925
43:09.440 --> 43:10.590
while cooking at home.
